{"id": "EUVD-2026-86661", "enisaUuid": "d3ac1f4e-b5da-377b-992a-61fd6e763052", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: macb: fix NULL pointer dereference on unbind with fixed-link\n\nWhen the device tree describes a fixed-link and has no \"mdio\" child\nnode, macb_mii_init() returns early without allocating the MDIO bus,\nleaving bp->mii_bus as NULL.\n\nTwo cleanup paths then dereference this NULL bus:\n\n1. On driver unbind, macb_remove() unconditionally calls\n   mdiobus_unregister(bp->mii_bus), which oopses:\n\n  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000000000004a8\n  pc : mdiobus_unregister+0x14/0xa4\n  lr : macb_remove+0x38/0xa4\n  Call trace:\n   mdiobus_unregister+0x14/0xa4 (P)\n   macb_remove+0x38/0xa4\n   platform_remove+0x20/0x30\n   device_release_driver_internal+0x1c8/0x224\n   unbind_store+0xb4/0xbc\n\n2. On the probe error path in macb_probe(), reached when\n   macb_mii_init() has succeeded but a subsequent step fails, the\n   err_out_unregister_mdio label runs the same unconditional cleanup.\n\nmdiobus_unregister() and mdiobus_free() do not guard against a NULL\nbus, so guard the calls in both macb_remove() and the probe error\npath.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/afa224cabc0132ca414b9141b1a919ca2d318cd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/054ad8e66025eb4778d840bef80c270646cebcd2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f737d999fcb8f276d77b01ea4c2016ee01dad19b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5710f6a74f63cbba0e15cd75917234916181c9d4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/edb39c7666bb3924da761dfb417db85c1e5d8ad3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38b6be101006d3e7af972999f45d4f1e8250587a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h4xg-972w-f7c3", "CVE-2026-98008"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0380e019-50a1-3a23-9a28-9d83099ef419", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cafa5942bd2df3d80e3eeb2deb4bc050f7761f3d"}, {"id": "1dda52a4-c4c2-3155-a873-210a39e5a57e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0c3601f2c4e12e7689b0f46ebc17525250ea8c3 <edb39c7666bb3924da761dfb417db85c1e5d8ad3"}, {"id": "22427a81-e0ca-3e58-9c72-2e90c5a884c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "2bcb8a10-3fe4-3fe6-a0a4-3b71df5a64f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.169 <5.16"}, {"id": "2d50ec58-1352-3062-bd80-dd6f213ac647", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19088c5378c9fea54e552d8bc7418a3aa1e06990"}, {"id": "4aa6c80b-8673-3e3c-a4b1-39354fa9fcaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.228 <5.11"}, {"id": "523362f9-7b31-3e11-bce0-54189b7fb3b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "5262c057-74b9-3c3d-b4d1-1124124e1769", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "52e8a19e-2142-300a-9d73-4e964e9e431d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0c3601f2c4e12e7689b0f46ebc17525250ea8c3 <38b6be101006d3e7af972999f45d4f1e8250587a"}, {"id": "59fbe202-5e9e-39cf-a473-3c047e47350e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c81dcaa9cd0b66816c2ecb6c5df0b6afde9c7da5"}, {"id": "6523c20b-9546-34da-a4d5-aa1f600a49e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "6b8f2fe9-7aef-38e0-9c44-157f9fec5944", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "6dd5f5e7-9542-309e-862b-e02d23ae5bf7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.114 <6.1.18